  "limitations": [
    "One seed and one generated data set per mobility case; repetitions time the same data.",
    "Synthetic balanced six-period unit-weight panels with Gaussian controls and roughly uniform firm sizes.",
    "Short panels and low mobility produce many low-degree workers and are well suited to the elimination step.",
    "Low-mobility cases can be disconnected; topology.csv reports components.",
    "Three timing repetitions and partial cyclic order provide exploratory medians, not confidence intervals or general speed guarantees.",
    "Tolerances are solver-specific; accepted fits need not have identical achieved error.",
    "Failed native gates vary in magnitude and do not all imply inaccurate slope coefficients.",
    "No peak-memory measurement, large administrative-data qualification or multi-platform benchmark.",
    "Withinr uses its own approximate Schur step; the comparison is between complete configured methods."
  ],
